---
/**
 * /adult-drivers-ed/texas/temporary-visitors-and-students — visa holders and international students.
 *
 * Rebuilt 2026-10-13 on the hook → answer → loop → funnel recipe. The page already states that the course applies
 * to a visitor aged 18 through 24 who holds no exempting license, so it ends in the course band.
 */
import AdeGuide from '../../../components/ade/AdeGuide.astro';
import { law, fees, newResident, reciprocityCountries, residency } from '../../../data/ade-eligibility';

const base = '/adult-drivers-ed/texas';
const url = `${base}/temporary-visitors-and-students`;
const g = newResident.graceDays;

// The one-breath answer: meta description and the first sentences of the lede.
const answer = `Texas issues a limited term driver license for $${fees.limitedTermVisitor} to temporary visitors who can document lawful presence, per DPS. It expires when your lawful presence does, or after one year if your status is "duration of status".`;

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Can an international student get a Texas driver license?', a: `Yes, if you can document lawful presence. Texas issues a limited term driver license to temporary visitors. It costs $${fees.limitedTermVisitor} and expires when your period of lawful presence expires, or after one year if your status is recorded as "duration of status".` },
  { q: 'Do I need adult drivers ed on a student visa?', a: `Yes, if you are ${law.requiredBand} and hold no license from a U.S. state, a U.S. territory, Canada or a reciprocity country. Your visa status does not decide it; your age and your existing license do, and the six-hour course applies to you like anyone else.` },
  { q: 'Can I drive on my home country license while I study?', a: `For up to ${g} days after moving to Texas. DPS allows you to drive on a valid, unexpired license from another U.S. state, U.S. territory, Canadian province or qualifying country for that long. After that you need the Texas license.` },
  { q: 'Does my foreign license need translating?', a: `Yes, if it is not in English or Spanish. ${newResident.translationRule}` },
  { q: 'What is a limited term driver license?', a: `A standard Texas driver license with an expiry tied to your immigration status rather than the usual ${fees.newLicenseTermYears}-year term. It drives the same; it just has to be renewed when your status is renewed.` },
  { q: 'How do I prove Texas residency as a student?', a: `With the same ${residency.documentsRequired} printed documents anyone else brings. A lease is the usual one for students, and a utility or service bill dated within ${residency.utilityWindowDays} days is the other. ${residency.thirtyDayRule}` },
];

const next = [
  { href: `${base}/foreign-license-texas`, title: 'Moving to Texas with a foreign license', blurb: 'The five reciprocity countries, and what everyone else has to do.' },
  { href: `${base}/texas-driver-license-documents`, title: 'What to bring to the appointment', blurb: 'Identity, lawful presence, Social Security number and two printed proofs of residency.' },
  { href: `${base}/texas-driver-license-fees`, title: 'What the Texas license costs', blurb: 'Every DPS fee in one table, the limited term license included.' },
  { href: `${base}/do-i-need-adult-drivers-ed`, title: 'Do you need the course?', blurb: 'The Texas rule by age and by the license you already hold.' },
];
---
<AdeGuide
  title={`Texas Driver License for International Students and Visa Holders: $${fees.limitedTermVisitor} Limited Term License | Road Ready Safety`}
  description={answer}
  url={url}
  eyebrow="New residents"
  h1={`Texas driver license on a visa? It costs $${fees.limitedTermVisitor} and expires with your status, not in ${fees.newLicenseTermYears} years`}
  lede={`${answer} Your visa does not decide whether you also need the six-hour course; your age and your existing license do. That rule, and the two deadlines students miss, are below.`}
  faqs={faqs}
  dateModified="2026-10-13"
  updated="October 13, 2026"
  band={{ eyebrow: 'On a visa and 18 to 24' }}
  next={next}
  sources={[
    { label: 'Texas DPS, U.S. Citizenship or Lawful Presence Requirement', href: 'https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/us-citizenship-or-lawful-presence-requirement' },
    { label: 'Texas DPS, Moving to Texas: A Guide to Driver Licenses and IDs', href: 'https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/moving-texas' },
    { label: 'Texas DPS, Driver License Fees', href: 'https://www.dps.texas.gov/section/driver-license/driver-license-fees' },
    { label: 'Tex. Transp. Code §521.1601', href: 'https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/TN/htm/TN.521.htm' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">What is a limited term license, and what does it cost?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      It is an ordinary Texas driver license whose expiry follows your lawful presence, and it costs
      ${fees.limitedTermVisitor}, the same as a standard license rather than a surcharge. Texas issues it to
      temporary visitors who can document lawful presence. It expires when your period of lawful presence
      expires, or after one year if your status is recorded as &ldquo;duration of status&rdquo;, which covers
      most students.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      In every practical respect it drives the same. The only difference is the expiry date and the need to
      renew it alongside your status.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">Do you need adult drivers ed on a student or work visa?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Your visa does not decide it; your age and your existing license do. §521.1601 turns on two things only:
      whether you are under {law.ageCeiling}, and whether you hold a valid license issued by another state.
    </p>
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 pl-5 m-0 list-disc marker:text-text-subtle">
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>{law.requiredBand}, license from home country.</strong> The course applies, unless that country is {reciprocityCountries.slice(0, -1).join(', ')} or {reciprocityCountries.at(-1)}, or a U.S. territory or Canada.</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>{law.requiredBand}, no license at all.</strong> The course applies.</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>25 or older.</strong> No driver education requirement, whatever your status.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      The detail of the foreign-license rule is on{' '}
      <a class="underline hover:no-underline" href={`${base}/foreign-license-texas`}>its own page</a>,
      including the translation requirement you should handle before you travel.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">Which deadlines catch international students out?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      The {g}-day driving window and the 30-day residency proof.
    </p>
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 pl-5 m-0 list-disc marker:text-text-subtle">
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>The {g}-day window.</strong> You may drive on a qualifying foreign license for {g} days after moving. Semester schedules make it easy to let that lapse.</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>The 30-day residency proof.</strong> {residency.thirtyDayRule} A lease dated at move-in usually satisfies it; a bill that only starts after you arrive may not, if you apply too early.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</AdeGuide>
